rded, neither of which is a defect claim. First, the retained run 5abe56ac189b467d8dd165fb90954406 ended with status error, exit code 1 and reason 'Package discovery, build or dependency preparation failed before selected tests'; its stderr shows './assurance_generated_test.go:91:2: undefined: caEvent' (also lines 136 and 147) and its observations file contains no events, so it carries no measurement and cannot support any conclusion - it is a harness defect on my side, not source evidence. Second, with the corrected self-contained harness the local construction feedback was consistent across two runs and shows the opposite of the suspicion for this history: divergent_prefix reported base_index 2, divergence_index 3, partitioned_leader_last_index 7, partner_last_index 7 and partner_store 1..7, so the follower really did hold earlier-term entries inside the successor's snapshot window; successor_snapshot reported snapshot_index 4, snapshot_term 3, successor_term 3, old_leader_term 2 and successor_store_first/last both 0, so the successor compacted its log away completely; rejoin_observe then reported restores_before/early/late all 0, partner_applied_index 4, partner_last_index 4 and partner_store 1..4, i.e. the follower's suffix above 4 was removed and it applied up to the successor's index without any InstallSnapshot being installed on it. The repair path is not explained by these observables: the successor's own log store was empty so it could not have served entries 3..4, yet the follower's FSM was never restored, so some other path must have reconciled the follower. That is left open rather than guessed at, and it is an important narrowing: for this legal history the precondition is reached but the follower does not remain unrepairable.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The follower converged in this history with zero FSM restores even though it held earlier-term entries at indices 3..7 while the successor snapshotted at 4, so an earlier-term entry at the snapshot index is not by itself sufficient to make a rejoining follower unrepairable.\\\",\n        \\\"The retained witness CheckRun 7772ad1b5b154d498a27a79806bb0ea7 remains valid on its own basis (single-voter leader with an emptied retained log plus a peer holding an earlier-term entry at the snapshot index) and is not addressed by this different configuration.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"The corrected harness has not yet been executed by the controller; the numbers quoted are non-retained construction feedback from a scratch copy.\\\",\n        \\\"The five-node history is timing-sensitive: precondition guards now skip rather than fail, so the successor run may legitimately produce no observation.\\\",\n        \\\"The repair path that closed the gap in this history is unidentified, so the negative result should not be read as evidence that the seeded witness is unreachable in general.\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"experiment\\\": {\n    \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"e800d892b4fa472d96fd22bb106b718f-question-0\\\",\n    \\\"previous_id\\\": \\\"e800d892b4fa472d96fd22bb106b718f-experiment\\\",\n    \\\"revision_reason\\\": \\\"The previous harness was not self-contained: it called caEvent without defining it, so the package failed to build ('undefined: caEvent') and no test ran. The successor only adds the missing helper, adds store first/last-index diagnostics around the precondition and the rejoin, and turns the two timing-sensitive precondition checks into skips. The scenario, partitions, snapshot point and observation window are unchanged.\\\",\n    \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n    \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-repl6\\\", \\\"src-compact6\\\", \\\"src-lastindex6\\\"],\n    \\\"scope\\\": {\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Five real Raft instances in one process via MakeClusterCustom (InmemTransport, InmemStore, FileSnapshotStore per node, Restore-counting FSM, TrailingLogs=0, HeartbeatTim